{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFw1jAfud2Qev5YN43dZ2G","type":"tool_result","content":"[test.TC-199]\nverifies = [\"SR-163\", \"LLR-203\"]\nlevel = \"Integration\"\nmethod = \"\"\"The inventory's two delivered finding classes, driven where each one can actually fail. THE DOGFOOD DIRECTION, in process against the live MAPPING literal: a declared destination that this repository neither carries nor serves in place out of the kit tree, and which no absence declaration covers, is reported by name; a declared absence whose destination has materialized is reported as stale, with the lifecycle marker exempting only the paths whose presence is a legal state; and the walk is bite-proofed by removing one declared entry and asserting its destination reappears in the finding set, so a walk that had quietly stopped looking could not pass. THE PACKAGE DIRECTION, asked of a REAL bootstrapped scaffold rather than of the kit tree, because the kit's own scripts directory holds every file and a partial copy reads green there: the copied helper package must hold exactly the kit's module set - a missing or stale MAPPING row is named as the cause - and must import from where a shipped script sits; and a shipped script importing a sibling the inventory omits is reported against the MAPPING literal read as an AST, never as a whole-file regex, so a comment naming a module cannot mark it mapped.\"\"\"\ntier = \"Full\"\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-203 (parent SR-163)\"\nautomated = \"Yes\"\nevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_dogfood_sync.py::test_scaffold_mapping_covered_or_declared; tests/test_dogfood_sync.py::test_scaffold_omissions_list_is_current; tests/test_dogfood_sync.py::test_bite_scaffold_walk_catches_an_undeclared_absence; tests/test_bootstrap.py::test_the_common_package_ships_complete; tests/test_bootstrap.py::test_every_sibling_imported_module_is_shipped_by_mapping\"\"\"\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\nphase = 5\n\n[test.TC-200]\nverifies = [\"SR-163\", \"LLR-204\"]\nlevel = \"Integration\"\nmethod = \"\"\"The grammar and the policy, separately, because they fail separately. THE GRAMMAR, driven directly on the shared function both the map column and the coverage percentage read, so a divergence between the two is unrepresentable: a declaration token opening a line yields its spine ids; prose naming ids without the token yields none; a token PRECEDED by prose yields none, including the two shapes that had previously harvested a sentence denying a link as a declaration of it; whitespace, comment markers and quote characters may precede the token and nothing else may; a wrapped list continuation line declares nothing. THE POLICY, driven through the real command line on a real bootstrapped scaffold rather than by reading the code: with a threshold declared in the policy home and a live design row that no source declaration names, the report prints the shortfall and exits ZERO, and only the explicit strict arm turns the same reading into a nonzero exit - which is what makes the threshold a gate a repository opts into rather than one the delivered package arms on its behalf.\"\"\"\ntier = \"Full\"\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-204 (parent SR-163)\"\nautomated = \"Yes\"\nevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_gen_arch_map.py::test_backlink_ids_is_the_one_definition_of_a_declaration; tests/test_gen_arch_map.py::test_backlink_cli_is_warn_first_and_strict_only_on_demand\"\"\"\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\nphase = 5\n\n[test.TC-201]\n=== LLR-203/204 ===\n2134:[design.LLR-203]\n2146:[design.LLR-204]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"621ad4b3-6278-4367-b820-9e5a6771d199","uuid":"c9b85e90-026f-49bc-ad4f-41d043ccc8f3","timestamp":"2026-08-30T09:11:05.638Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"[test.TC-199]\nverifies = [\"SR-163\", \"LLR-203\"]\nlevel = \"Integration\"\nmethod = \"\"\"The inventory's two delivered finding classes, driven where each one can actually fail. THE DOG